NAME
    rdline - read one line of the input (#include "../lib_rdline.c")

SYNOPSIS
    #include "../lib_rdline.c"    (includes lib_stdin.c)
    char buf[256];
    while (readline(buf)) ...

DESCRIPTION
    readline(buf) reads the next line of the lib_stdin stream (see
    stdin) through nextc() into buf, NUL-terminated, and returns 1, or
    0 when the input had already ended. LF ends the line and is not
    stored; CR is dropped, so CR LF and LF sources read alike. A last
    line with no LF still returns 1.

LIMITS
    255 characters are kept; the rest of a longer line is read and
    dropped, so the next call starts at the next line. buf must hold
    256 bytes.

NOTES
    Used by grep, sed and uniq (awk has a reader of its own).
    Unchanged from the P8X version but for the #include: lib_rdline.c
    includes lib_stdin.c itself, so there is no order of //#use lines
    to keep.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/lib_rdline.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    stdin, grep, sed, uniq
